How can I add decision-making capabilities to the QueueController class to handle enqueue and dequeue operations based on certain conditions?

To add decision-making capabilities to the QueueController class, you can introduce methods that evaluate the conditions before enqueuing or dequeuing messages. Below is a sample implementation:

```java
package com.harbor.queue;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/queue")
public class QueueController {
    private Queue<String> queue = new LinkedList<>();

    @PostMapping("/enqueue")
    public ResponseEntity<String> enqueue(@RequestBody String message) {
        if (queue.size() < 10) { // Limit the queue size
            queue.offer(message);
            return ResponseEntity.ok("Enqueued: " + message);
        } else {
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN).body("Queue is full");
        }
    }

    @GetMapping("/dequeue")
    public ResponseEntity<String> dequeue() {
        String message = queue.poll();
        if (message != null) {
            return ResponseEntity.ok("Dequeued: " + message);
        } else {
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body("Queue is empty");
        }
    }
}
```

Additionally, update the `application.properties` file to set the maximum queue size:

```
queue.max.size=10
```

These changes will allow the QueueController to handle enqueue and dequeue operations more intelligently based on the current state of the queue.

