How can I implement cascading configurations where a higher priority setting overrides lower priority ones in CascadeConfig.java?

To implement cascading configurations, you can use a map to hold your settings with their corresponding priority levels. When retrieving a configuration, check from the highest to the lowest priority. Here's a code snippet to illustrate this:

```java
public class CascadeConfig {
    private Map<Integer, Map<String, String>> configs;

    public CascadeConfig() {
        configs = new TreeMap<>(Collections.reverseOrder()); // Higher priorities go first
    }

    public void addConfig(int priority, Map<String, String> config) {
        configs.put(priority, config);
    }

    public String getConfigValue(String key) {
        for (Map<String, String> config : configs.values()) {
