How can I ensure there are no cyclical dependencies in my flag resolution?

You can track visited flags during resolution. Modify your `resolve` method to accept an array of visited flags:

```javascript
resolve(flagId, visited = []) {
  if (visited.includes(flagId)) {
    throw new Error('Cyclical dependency detected!');
  }
  visited.push(flagId);
  const flag = this.flags[flagId];
  if (!flag) return null;
  if (flag.dependsOn) {
    return this.resolve(flag.dependsOn, visited);
  }
  return flag.value;
}
```
This prevents infinite loops during flag resolution.

